# Secrets ??? .env.example is checked in, .env never is (??9.8)
.env

# The build log behind the submission answer "What broke, and how you got out"
# (??0.1). A working document ??? kept local, never committed, never pushed.
broke_fixed.txt

# The two spec documents this build was written against ??? the implementation
# guide and the review guide. Local working documents. They were tracked between
# 64c1e95 and gate 11 and have been removed from the index and purged from
# history; this line is what stops them coming back on the next `git add -A`.
docs/

# Generated datasets. Reproducible from a seed, so never committed (§2.7 rule 2)
# — except the two the hosted demo serves, which must exist in the image
# because a container cannot run `make generate` on boot. 72 KB each, and
# still reproducible: `make generate SEED=42` rewrites them byte for byte.
data/
# The eight the hosted demo serves. 72 KB each, and still reproducible —
# `python tasks.py generate --seed N` rewrites any of them byte for byte.
# Seed 42 is the demo, 7 is the held-out one, 1-5 are the multi-seed spread
# the README reports mean +/- std over, 99 is a spare.
!data/seed1/
!data/seed1/**
!data/seed2/
!data/seed2/**
!data/seed3/
!data/seed3/**
!data/seed4/
!data/seed4/**
!data/seed5/
!data/seed5/**
!data/seed7/
!data/seed7/**
!data/seed42/
!data/seed42/**
!data/seed99/
!data/seed99/**
build/

